# --- undo the repo root's blanket exclusions -------------------------------
# The root .gitignore has `*.json`, `*.png` and `*.pt`, which are right for the
# C++/OpenFHE side of this repo but would silently drop EVERY result file in this
# subtree -- metrics.json, config.json, the fitted coefficients, the Part 4 plot.
# Negate them here, then re-exclude the specific bulk further down.
!*.json
!*.png

# --- virtualenv / caches ---------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# --- job logs: noisy, and they embed absolute cluster paths ----------------
logs/
*.log

# --- regenerable bulk ------------------------------------------------------
# The RESULT files (csv / metrics.json / config.json) and the 130m fitted
# coefficients ARE committed -- they are the deliverable, and they let you
# reproduce the per-head polynomials with no GPU via --coeff-json.
# What is excluded here is large and regenerable:
#   transition_stats.json for the bigger models holds per-head arrays for
#   thousands of heads; the per-model coefficient dumps likewise. Rebuild with
#       python collect_transition_stats.py --model <model> --blocks 64
runs/gpu/e2_scale/*/stats/transition_stats.json
runs/gpu/e2_scale/*/sweep/polynomial_coefficients.json
runs/gpu/e1_cross_domain/fit_stats/
runs/_smoke/
runs/part7_zero_training_full/

# trained tensors from --save-weights
*.pt
